From b3269af2110e01b2c710f83ea287425939a9b4d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:15:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban quota recovery: no proof-gate bench without a
 failed proof; test the SubprocessError catch

Follow-up to the two non-blocking nits in review 5889821623 on PR #2101.

1. recover() reserved the 10-min proof-gate row (quota_proof_gate.db, per
   provider/model/account) for every eligible account before its deadline
   early return, and a proof that succeeded after the deadline (loop break or
   as_completed timeout) kept its row. Either way the account stayed benched
   600 s with no failed proof behind it.
   Fix: check the deadline before reserving; if it passes during the
   reservation, release every reserved row; and settle each proof future with a
   done callback that releases the row when the proof succeeded (late included)
   or was cancelled unstarted. Only a proof that ran and did not succeed keeps
   its row; a late success still never clears the bench.

2. completion_succeeds' SubprocessError catch had no test of its own. New test
   raises subprocess.SubprocessError from the resolver spawn (the probe path's
   Popen) and asserts the proof reads False.

Proof (hermes-core-wt test, worker-5):
- RED on origin/main sources (SubprocessError clause dropped for nit 2):
  test_expired_deadline_reserves_no_proof,
  test_deadline_lost_during_reservation_releases_rows,
  test_successful_late_proof_releases_its_row,
  test_completion_returns_false_when_resolver_spawn_raises_subprocess_error
  all FAIL.
- GREEN: 17 quota files, 293 passed. scripts/check --base origin/main: 19 checks ok.
